{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "NAM",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to the bloody city! it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all full of lies ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " robberies; the prey departeth not;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The noise of a whip, and the noise of the rattling of the wheels, and of the prancing horses, and of the bounding chariots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The horseman lifteth up both the bright sword, and the glittering spear: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a multitude of slain, and a great number of carcasses; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no end of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " corpses; they stumble upon their corpses:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because of the multitude of the lewd deeds of the well-favored harlot, the mistress of witchcrafts, that selleth nations through her lewd deeds, and families through her witchcrafts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against thee, saith the LORD of hosts; and I will remove thy skirts upon thy face, and I will show the nations thy nakedness, and the kingdoms thy shame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will cast abominable filth upon thee, and make thee vile, and will set thee as a gazing-stock.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall come to pass, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all they that look upon thee shall flee from thee, and say, Nineveh is laid waste: who will bemoan her; whence shall I seek comforters for thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Art thou better than populous No, that was situated among the rivers, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that had",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the waters around it, whose rampart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the sea, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " her wall ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the sea?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Cush and Egypt ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " her strength, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " infinite; Put and Lubim were thy helpers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " she carried away, she went into captivity: her young children also were dashed in pieces at the head of all the streets: and they cast lots for her honorable men, and all her great men were bound in chains.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou also shalt be drunken: thou shalt be hid, thou also shalt seek strength because of the enemy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All thy strong holds ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fig-trees with the first ripe figs: if they be shaken, they shall even fall into the mouth of the eater.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thy people in the midst of thee ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " women: the gates of thy land shall be set wide open to thy enemies: the fire shall devour thy bars.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Draw thee waters for the siege, fortify thy strong holds: go into clay, and tread the mortar, make strong the brick-kiln.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There shall the fire devour thee; the sword shall cut thee off, it shall eat thee up like the canker-worm: make thyself many as the canker-worm, make thyself many as the locusts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast multiplied thy merchants above the stars of heaven: the canker-worm spoileth, and flieth away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy crowned ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as the locusts, and thy captains as the great grasshoppers, which settle in the hedges in the cold day, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " when the sun ariseth they flee away, and their place is not known where they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy shepherds slumber, O king of Assyria: thy nobles shall dwell ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the dust",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": thy people are scattered upon the mountains, and no man gathereth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NAM.3.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NAM.3.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no healing of thy bruise; thy wound is grievous: all that hear the fame of thee shall clap the hands over thee: for upon whom hath not thy wickedness passed continually?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
